# The build context for every deploy/ Dockerfile is the repository root, not
# the module directory: each service module declares
# `replace github.com/booleanism/surr => ../`, so building `hub/` needs the
# root module's internal/ tree sitting next to it. That makes this file the
# only thing standing between a build and a multi-gigabyte context.
.git
.github
.cache
.venv
bin
**/__pycache__
*.py[cod]
# Model weights are downloaded by the node on first use and live in a volume,
# so they are never baked into an image (and .gitignore keeps them out of the
# repository too).
weights
*.pt
# Local databases. The containers use their own volume-mounted files.
*.db
*.db-shm
*.db-wal
# The deploy directory itself is not needed inside any image.
deploy
